EXT. TUG-OF-WAR PIT - COUNTY FAIR - DUSK

Mud. Two ropes of frayed hemp. A line of chalk. Four people in team shirts stand knee-deep in the slop.

HOLLIS BRANDT hauls the knot. NEELA CHOWDHURY braces her heels. TOBY MARCINKIEWICZ squints at the opposing team across the pit. WENDOLYN ACHTERBERG spits and tightens her grip.

HOLLIS
On three.

TOBY
On two.

NEELA
On three!

WENDOLYN
Whatever, just pull!

The horn sounds. The rope snaps taut. They lean back as one.

HOLLIS
Heave!

NEELA ^
Heave!

TOBY
Don't let go!

WENDOLYN
Don't you dare!

Hollis's boot slides. Neela grabs his belt. Toby's grip slips. Wendolyn screams.

HOLLIS
Left!

TOBY
Right!

NEELA
Down!

WENDOLYN
Up!

The rope goes slack. All four fall backward into the mud with a splat. They lie there, eyes toward the sky.

Hollis wipes his face. Neela stares at her hands. Toby laughs once, short. Wendolyn closes her eyes.

Nobody says who won.
